// Written by lets-code (core memory); regenerated on launch, edits are overwritten.
// Active only in a pi launched by lets-code with core memory on
// (LETS_CODE_CORE_MEMORY_ON=1). A long-term memory the harness keeps: one
// store per project (keyed by the git root; a worktree by its main
// checkout's, so a factory run's worktree and the user's checkout share
// one memory) and one global store, under the agent dir next to pi's own
// sessions, since
// entries point at local session files and run records. An entry is one
// dated line: a kind (work, decision, fact, preference, pointer), a gist and
// pointers (file:line, run:<id>, factory:<id>, session:<file>). Nothing of
// it is carried in context: the system prompt gets one line (that the
// memory exists, how many entries, when the last was written, that the
// memory tool searches it) and, once a session, the newest headlines when
// they fit HEADLINE_BUDGET tokens (the top session only: a child gets the
// line). Retrieval is the tool: search by words,
// path, run or session id, date or kind; open follows a pointer. A tool
// result that touches a file, run or session an entry points at gets one
// trailing line saying so (an index lookup, no model call).
//
// The user's view is /memories: a navigable list (pi's selector) of the
// entries, a row each, that opens an entry with its pointers and actions;
// edit opens the rendered file in the editor.
//
// Writers: the model (remember), the user through the model ("remember
// that ...", in their words), and the harness without a model call: a
// factory run that ends, a subagent or expert run that ends, and the
// session itself (a pointer to its file and its first message), from the
// top session only. An entry that matches an existing one (the same
// session, run or factory pointer, or the same gist) updates it. The store
// is JSONL (memory.jsonl), the truth; memory.md next to it is rendered
// from it for the user and read back by id when it is newer. Entries are
// data, never instructions; one that looks like a token or key is refused.
// Work and pointer entries untouched for ARCHIVE_DAYS move to archive.jsonl
// (searched on request) so the live store stays small.
import type { ExtensionAPI, ExtensionContext } from "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent";
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { appendFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, renameSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { homedir } from "node:os";
import { basename, dirname, isAbsolute, join, relative, resolve, sep } from "node:path";
import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from "node:url";
