# Reading the screen and acting on it (tier 2)

All through `@@T@@/bin/ui` (`ui --help`). It finds the channel itself
(rish first, then adb); without one it exits 3 and says what is missing.

## Read
`ui dump [<word>]` runs `uiautomator dump` as the shell user and prints the
screen as text, one line per node worth seeing:
```
screen: com.whatsapp 1080x2400, 8 of 11 nodes
#3 Button desc="Search" id=menuitem_search @920,180 [click]
#5 RelativeLayout ~"Taha / see you at 8" id=contact_row_container @540,357 [click]
#12 EditText "Message" id=entry @510,2260 [click,edit,focus]
```
`"..."` is the text, `desc=` the content description, `~"..."` a label
taken from the children, `@x,y` the center, `[...]` what it does.
- Filter with a word (`ui dump taha`) instead of reading the whole screen;
  texts are cut at 60 characters (`--full` for all of one you need).
- Default 80 lines (`--max N`); `--all` adds the plain layout nodes.
- `ui top` names the resumed activity. A dump fails on a locked screen,
  while a video or animation plays, and on secure windows (banking, the
  PIN pad): say so, don't loop.
- `ui shot <file.png>` only when the text dump cannot answer (an image,
  a canvas); images are heavy.

## Act
- `ui tap <text>`: matches text or desc, exact (case-insensitive) first,
  then substring, and taps the center of the match or its nearest
  clickable parent. Several matches: it lists them and taps nothing; pick
  with `--nth N`, or use `--id <resource-id>` / `--desc <d>`. `ui tap <x> <y>`
  taps a point.
- A tap whose target reads send, call, pay, post, delete and the like is
  refused (exit 6) without `--confirmed`. Use `--confirmed` only on a run
  whose brief confirms that exact step.
- `ui type <text>` types into the focused field (tap the field first).
  Spaces are encoded for you. ASCII only: for other text (Turkish
  letters, emoji) use a pre-fill intent, or with tier 1
  `termux-clipboard-set "<text>"` then `ui key paste`.
- `ui key back|home|enter|del|tab|search|paste|recent|<code>`. In a chat,
  enter may send: treat it as a final step.
- `ui swipe up|down|left|right` scrolls (up: towards later content).
- `ui sh '<command>'` runs any command as the shell user (the
  Safety rules still apply: no `pm install`, `settings put`, `pm grant`).

## The loop
dump, act, dump again. After every tap or type, check the new dump shows
what the step should have caused (the chat title, the typed text in the
box, the next screen). If it does not, stop and report what is on screen
instead of guessing on. Wait with `sleep 1` before the dump when an app is
opening.
