# Termux:API: every command, by category

Tier 1 only: call these only when the probe says `tier 1 termux-api: yes`.
The commands talk to the Termux:API app; without it they hang, even when
`pkg termux-api` is installed. Read the category the goal needs, not all.

## Rules for every call
- **Wrap it:** `timeout 20 termux-<cmd> ...`. A hang (rc 124) means the
  app is missing, a permission prompt is waiting on the phone, or (for
  location) no fix yet. Stop and say which; do not loop.
- **Output:** reads print JSON (parse with `python3 -c` or `jq`); actions
  print nothing and rc 0. An error comes back as JSON with an `error` key,
  or as a line naming the missing permission.
- **Permissions:** the first call that needs one opens Android's prompt on
  the phone (the user taps Allow). Denied: the command fails or returns
  nothing; tell the user where to allow it (Settings > Apps > Termux:API >
  Permissions). Special access (below) is a settings screen, not a prompt.
- **Needs the user (UI):** marked "UI": shows a dialog, picker or activity
  on the phone, so the screen must be on and unlocked, and the call blocks
  until the user answers.
- **Private** (marked): read only what the goal needs, filter before you
  print, report only that item (the Privacy section of your agent file).
- **Final steps** (marked): reach other people, cost money or cannot be
  undone: only with the brief's `confirmed` (the Consent section).
- **Changes** (marked): change device state; do exactly what the goal asks,
  read the before value where a read exists, never on your own.

## Prefer it over hand-rolled commands
| task | use | not |
|---|---|---|
| battery level, charging | `termux-battery-status` | `dumpsys battery`, /sys files |
| clipboard | `termux-clipboard-get` / `-set` | `ui type`, `am broadcast` |
| show the user something | `termux-toast`, `termux-notification` | (tier 0 has nothing) |
| ask the user | `termux-dialog` | a chat question when they are at the phone |
| where am I | `termux-location -p network -r last` | IP geolocation |
| a contact's number | `termux-contact-list` filtered | `content query` (tier 2) |
| volume | `termux-volume` | `cmd audio`, `media volume` |
| wifi network | `termux-wifi-connectioninfo` | `dumpsys wifi` |
| open a URL | `termux-open-url` (core, no app) | — |
| speak text | `termux-tts-speak` | — |
Evidence: a read's JSON is the evidence (`api-read`). An action (toast,
notification, vibrate, torch) prints nothing: its rc 0 is
`system-accepted` only when the channel's control,
`timeout 20 termux-battery-status`, prints JSON. A bad flag is no control
(the script rejects it before the app is reached). You cannot see a toast:
say it was sent, not seen. A notification you can check with
`termux-notification-list` (needs Notification access).

## Device state and sensors
- `termux-battery-status`: JSON percentage, status, plugged, health,
  temperature, current. No permission.
- `termux-audio-info`: audio output, sample rate, buffer sizes; whether
  music is playing. No permission.
- `termux-volume` (no args): JSON of each stream's volume and max.
  `termux-volume <alarm|music|notification|ring|system|call> <n>`: sets
  one (Changes). In Do Not Disturb, ring/notification may need DND access.
- `termux-brightness <0-255|auto>`: screen brightness (Changes). Special
  access: "Modify system settings" for Termux:API (first use opens it).
- `termux-torch <on|off>`: the flashlight (Changes). No permission.
- `termux-vibrate [-d ms] [-f]`: vibrate (default 1000 ms; `-f` even in
  silent mode). VIBRATE (no prompt).
- `termux-sensor -l`: list sensors. `-s <name[,name]> -n 1`: one reading
  (partial names match). Without `-n` it streams forever; `-a` all sensors
  (battery cost); `-c` releases them after an interrupted run.
- `termux-camera-info`: JSON per camera (id, facing, sizes). No prompt.
- `termux-camera-photo [-c id] <file.jpg>`: takes a photo, no preview
  (Private; CAMERA). Some phones give a dark first shot.
- `termux-microphone-record -f <file> [-l secs] [-e aac|opus|amr_wb|amr_nb]`:
  records in the background (Private; RECORD_AUDIO). `-i` info, `-q` stop.
  Always give `-l` or stop it with `-q`.
- `termux-location [-p gps|network|passive] [-r once|last|updates]`: JSON
  latitude, longitude, accuracy (Private; ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION, and
  location must be on). gps indoors can take minutes: try `-p network` or
  `-r last` first; `-r updates` streams forever.
- `termux-infrared-frequencies`: the IR blaster's ranges (empty: none).
  `termux-infrared-transmit -f <hz> <on,off,...µs>`: sends a pattern
  under 2 s (Changes a device, e.g. a TV).
- `termux-fingerprint [-t title] [-d desc]`: UI; asks for a fingerprint;
  JSON `auth_result` (AUTH_RESULT_SUCCESS / _FAILURE). Android 6+.
- `termux-wifi-connectioninfo`: JSON ssid, bssid, ip, link speed, rssi.
  The SSID shows as `<unknown ssid>` without location permission and
  location on.
- `termux-wifi-scaninfo`: the last scan's networks (ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION,
  location on; Android throttles scans, so it may be old).
- `termux-wifi-enable <true|false>`: wifi on or off (Changes); newer
  Android may ignore it: then open `android.settings.WIFI_SETTINGS`.
- `termux-telephony-deviceinfo`: JSON operator, SIM state, network type,
  phone type (READ_PHONE_STATE).
- `termux-telephony-cellinfo`: the serving and nearby cells, signal
  (ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION).

## Communication
- `termux-contact-list`: every contact as JSON `[{name, number}]`
  (Private; READ_CONTACTS). Filter by name in python and print only the
  match: `timeout 20 termux-contact-list | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print([c for c in json.load(sys.stdin) if "taha" in c["name"].lower()])'`.
  Several matches: names only, and ask.
- `termux-call-log [-l n] [-o offset]`: the latest calls (default 10):
  name, number, type, date, duration (Private; READ_CALL_LOG).
- `termux-sms-list [-l n] [-o offset] [-t all|inbox|sent|draft|outbox|failed|queued] [-f number] [-c]`:
  messages as JSON (Private; READ_SMS). `-c` one per conversation. Default
  10 messages; keep `-l` small. (`termux-sms-inbox` is the old name: it
  only prints that.)
- `termux-sms-send -n <number[,number]> [-s slot] <text>`: sends at once,
  no screen (Final step; SEND_SMS; may cost money). Prefer the tier 0
  `smsto:` pre-fill unless `confirmed`.
- `termux-telephony-call <number>`: calls at once (Final step;
  CALL_PHONE). Prefer the tier 0 `DIAL` pre-fill.

## UI and notifications
- `termux-toast [-s] [-g top|middle|bottom] [-b color] [-c color] <text>`:
  a short popup on the phone. No permission. Text from args or stdin.
- `termux-notification -t <title> -c <text> [--id <id>] [--priority high] [--sound] [--vibrate 500,200]`:
  a notification (Android 13+: POST_NOTIFICATIONS prompt). Buttons:
  `--button1 <label> --button1-action '<shell cmd>'`; `--action` on tap;
  `--ongoing` pins it (needs `--id`); `--image-path`; `--type media` adds
  media buttons; `--channel <id>`. Actions run with `dash -c` later, so
  their output is lost: make them show it (`... | termux-toast`).
- `termux-notification-remove <id>`: removes one you posted with `--id`.
- `termux-notification-channel <id> <name>` / `-d <id>`: creates or deletes
  a channel (Android 8+).
- `termux-notification-list`: every notification shown, as JSON (Private;
  special access: Settings > Notifications > Device & app notifications >
  Termux:API). Filter to the one the goal names.
- `termux-dialog <widget> [-t title] [...]`: UI; asks the user, prints JSON
  `{code, text}` (cancel: code -2). Widgets: `confirm -i <question>`
  (text yes/no), `text [-i hint] [-m | -n] [-p]`, `radio|spinner|sheet -v "a,b,c"`,
  `checkbox -v "a,b,c"`, `counter -r min,max,start`, `date [-d format]`,
  `time`, `speech`. `termux-dialog -l` lists them.
- `termux-share [-a send|view|edit] [-c mime] [-d] [-t title] [file]`: UI;
  shares a file, or stdin as text, through Android's chooser (`-d`: the
  default app).
- `termux-wallpaper -f <file> | -u <url> [-l]`: sets the wallpaper, `-l`
  the lock screen (Changes; can't be read back).
- Core (termux-tools, no Termux:API app needed, tier 0):
  `termux-open-url <url>`, `termux-open [--send|--chooser] [--content-type t] <file|url>`
  (files in ~ need `allow-external-apps`: see your Traps).

## Clipboard
- `termux-clipboard-get`: the clipboard text (Private). Android 10+ may
  give nothing unless Termux is in the foreground.
- `termux-clipboard-set <text>` (or stdin): sets it (Changes: it replaces
  what the user copied). With tier 2: set it, then `ui key paste` to type
  non-ASCII text.

## Storage and media
- `termux-download [-t title] [-d desc] [-p path] <url>`: Android's
  download manager, with its notification; default folder Download.
- `termux-storage-get <out-file>`: UI; the user picks a file in the system
  picker, it is copied to out-file.
- `termux-media-scan [-r] [-v] <file...>`: makes files on /sdcard show in
  the gallery and music apps.
- `termux-media-player play <file> | play | pause | stop | info`: plays
  audio in the background (Termux:API's service).
- SAF (folders the user granted, also SD cards and cloud providers;
  URIs, not paths):
  `termux-saf-managedir` (UI; the user picks a folder; prints its URI),
  `termux-saf-dirs` (the granted folders), `termux-saf-ls <uri>`,
  `termux-saf-stat <uri>`, `termux-saf-read <uri> > file`,
  `termux-saf-write <uri> < file` (overwrites), `termux-saf-create [-t mime] <dir-uri> <name>`,
  `termux-saf-mkdir <dir-uri> <name>`, `termux-saf-rm <uri>` (Final step:
  deletes).

## System and background
- `termux-job-scheduler -s <script> [--job-id n] [--period-ms ms] [--network any|unmetered] [--charging true] [--persisted true]`:
  runs a script later or periodically (minimum period 15 min);
  `-p` pending jobs, `--cancel --job-id n`, `--cancel-all` (Changes).
- `termux-wake-lock` / `termux-wake-unlock` (core): keep the CPU awake for
  long Termux jobs; unlock afterwards (battery).
- `termux-keystore list [-d] | generate <alias> [-a RSA|EC] [-s bits] | sign <alias> <alg> | verify <alias> <alg> <sigfile> | delete <alias>`:
  keys in the hardware keystore that never leave it; `delete` is a Final
  step.
- `termux-nfc -r short|full` / `-w -t <text>`: UI; waits for a tag to be
  held to the phone (NFC must be on).
- `termux-usb -l`: USB devices; `-r <device>` asks the user for access
  (UI); `-e <cmd> <device>` runs cmd with the device's fd.
- `termux-speech-to-text [-p]`: listens on the mic and prints the text
  (Private; RECORD_AUDIO; needs a speech service).
- `termux-tts-engines`: TTS engines as JSON. `termux-tts-speak [-e engine] [-l lang] [-r rate] [-p pitch] [-s stream] <text>`:
  says it aloud.
- `termux-api-start` / `termux-api-stop`: start or stop Termux:API's
  keep-alive service; try a start when calls time out right after the app
  was killed.
