- Methods: the wrong method (405), HEAD and OPTIONS where relevant, CORS
  headers when the API is used from browsers.
- Idempotency and state: PUT and DELETE repeated give the same state;
  POST twice (duplicate?); concurrent writes; operations out of order;
  read after delete (404).
- Collections: empty, one, many; pagination edges (first, last, past the
  end, size 0 and huge), sorting and filters with odd values.
- Errors and limits: 404 for a missing id and a malformed id, rate limits
  (429 and its headers) only if the brief allows probing them, timeouts.
- GraphQL: the schema by introspection (if enabled, and whether it should
  be), each query and mutation's errors array and partial data, query
  depth and cost limits, field-level authorization.

