# Mobile (Appium) cheat sheet: element-repository 0.3.2

## What is supported
- `@civitas-cerebrum/element-repository` works with a WebdriverIO `Browser` (Appium session) as well as a Playwright `Page`. Elements come back as `PlatformElement`.
- The Steps API (`@civitas-cerebrum/element-interactions`, `baseFixture`, `steps.*`) is Playwright-only. Achilles' lifecycle is web-only. For mobile, use `ElementRepository` + the `Element` methods directly, with your own asserts.

## Constructor
```ts
import { ElementRepository, isPlatform, PlatformElement } from '@civitas-cerebrum/element-repository';
const repo = new ElementRepository(driver, 'tests/data/page-repository.json', 15000);
// (driver: WebdriverIO Browser | Playwright Page, pathOrParsedJson, defaultTimeout ms = 15000)
```

## page-repository.json with platform
`platform`: `"web"` (default if omitted), `"android"`, `"ios"`. The same page `name` can appear once per platform.
```json
{ "pages": [
  { "name": "LoginPage", "platform": "android", "elements": [
    { "elementName": "emailInput",   "selector": { "id": "com.example:id/email" } },
    { "elementName": "submitButton", "selector": { "accessibility id": "SubmitBtn" } },
    { "elementName": "title",        "selector": { "uiautomator": "new UiSelector().text(\"Login\")" } },
    { "elementName": "anyButton",    "selector": { "class name": "android.widget.Button" } }
  ]},
  { "name": "LoginPage", "platform": "ios", "elements": [
    { "elementName": "submitButton", "selector": { "predicate": "label == \"Submit\"" } },
    { "elementName": "allButtons",   "selector": { "class chain": "**/XCUIElementTypeButton" } }
  ]}
]}
```
Mobile keys (camelCase alias): `accessibility id` (`accessibilityId`) -> `~v`; `xpath` (raw); `id` -> `#v`; `uiautomator` (`androidUIAutomator`) -> `android=v`; `predicate` (`iOSNsPredicateString`); `class chain` (`iOSClassChain`); `class name` (`className`). `role`+`name` and `text` regex also map to UiSelector (Android) and predicates (iOS).

## Repository methods (elementName, pageName)
`get`, `getAll`, `getRandom`, `getByText(el, page, text)`, `getByAttribute(el, page, attr, value)`, `getByIndex(el, page, i)`, `getVisible`, `getByRole`, `getSelector`, `getSelectorRaw`, `getPagePlatform(page)`. `get*` returning `Element | null` take `strict` (true = throw instead of null).

## Element interface
Actions (return `Promise<Element>`, optional `{ timeout }`): `click`, `fill(text)`, `clear`, `check`, `uncheck`, `hover`, `doubleClick`, `scrollIntoView`, `pressSequentially(text, delay?)`. Web only: `setInputFiles`, `dispatchEvent`.
State/data: `isVisible()`, `isEnabled()`, `isChecked()`, `textContent()`, `getAttribute(name)`, `inputValue()`, `count()`, `all()`, `first()`, `nth(i)`, `filter({ hasText })`, `locateChild(sel)`, `raw()`, `waitFor({ state })` (visible|hidden|attached|detached).
Chain: `await el.action(5000).waitForState('visible').click()`; also `verifyPresence()`, `verifyText(t)`, `verifyTextContains(t)`, `getText()`.

