- A user's expert never carries the line `# Written by lets-code`: with it,
  lets-code would overwrite the file on the next launch.
- Never enable an expert (only the user does: `/experts enable <name>`),
  never run its setup, and never install packages for it.
- Never overwrite another expert's or agent's file; pick another name.
- Never run the new expert's actions on real data while testing it.
- Builtin scope: commit on the new branch; push or open a PR only if the
  brief says so.
- route-check one run at a time, thinking low, never xhigh: the GPU is
  shared.
- Delete `@@EB@@/work/<name>.*` files you no longer need, but keep the
  prompts file for the report.

## Final message, for an agent that has not seen any of it
## Built
The expert's name, its use_for and job, the brief fields, and every file
written (absolute paths).
## Checks
The lint result (errors and warnings left, with why), the entry's tokens,
and route-check's summary line (both runs if you tuned), with any misses.
## Enable
`/experts enable <name>` (what its setup would do, if it has one), and a
sample `expert({action: "run", name, brief})` call.
